PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U5.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":5,"theme":"Have You Ever…?","essential_question":"How do new experiences change us?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1","title":"Have You Ever Flown? The Present Perfect for Experiences","objectives":["Students will be able to form the present perfect with have/has + past participle.","Students will be able to ask and answer about life experiences with ever and never.","I can say \"I have visited Madinah\" and \"I've never seen snow.\"","I can ask \"Have you ever ridden a camel?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين المضارع التام باستخدام have/has + التصريف الثالث.","سيتمكن الطلاب من السؤال والإجابة عن تجارب الحياة باستخدام ever وnever.","أستطيع أن أقول I have visited Madinah وI've never seen snow.","أستطيع أن أسأل Have you ever ridden a camel?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪriəns/","definition":"something that happens to you that you remember","arabic":"تجربة","example":"Flying in a hot-air balloon was a great experience.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W01"},{"word":"ever","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɛvɚ/","definition":"at any time in your life (in questions)","arabic":"من قبل / في أي وقت","example":"Have you ever seen a shooting star?","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W02"},{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time","arabic":"أبدًا / قطّ","example":"I have never been to Japan.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W03"},{"word":"once","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/wʌns/","definition":"one time","arabic":"مرة واحدة","example":"I have ridden a horse once.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use the present perfect to talk about experiences in our life up to now. We don't say when they happened: I have visited Abha. (sometime in my life)\nForm: have / has + past participle. Regular verbs: past participle = -ed (visited, tried). Irregular verbs have special forms: be → been, see → seen, eat → eaten, fly → flown, ride → ridden, swim → swum.\nUse ever in questions (Have you ever…?) and never for \"not at any time\" (I've never…). Short forms: I've, she's, haven't, hasn't.\nI / you / we / they + have ('ve) + past participle\nhe / she / it + has ('s) + past participle\nHave you ever…? – Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.\nnever = not at any time: I've never been to Japan.","examples":["I've ridden a camel in the desert.","My sister has never seen snow.","Have you ever tried scuba diving?","We've visited Al-Ula twice.","My grandpa has flown in a helicopter.","Has your brother ever won a medal? – Yes, he has.","I haven't eaten Japanese food.","They've met the governor of Taif."],"common_errors":["✗ I have went to Abha. → ✓ I have been to Abha. (Use the past participle (been), not the past simple.)","✗ She have tried it. → ✓ She has tried it. (he/she/it → has.)","✗ Did you ever ride a camel? (life experience) → ✓ Have you ever ridden a camel? (Experiences → present perfect.)","✗ I have never not seen snow. → ✓ I have never seen snow. (never is already negative.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم المضارع التام للتحدث عن التجارب في حياتنا حتى الآن دون ذكر الوقت: I have visited Abha.\nالتركيب: have/has + التصريف الثالث (past participle): seen, eaten, flown, been.\nنستخدم ever في السؤال (Have you ever…?) وnever للنفي (I've never…).\nلا نقول I have went، بل I have been."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Have You Ever Flown? The Present Perfect for Experiences”. Let’s learn present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U5-LS1 | Have You Ever Flown? The Present Perfect for Experiences","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Uncle Fahad's Adventures”: Omar's uncle Fahad is a pilot, so he has visited many countries. He has worked for the same airline for fifteen years, and he has never missed a flight. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Omar's uncle Fahad is a pilot, so he has visited many countries. He has worked for the same airline for fifteen years, and he has never missed a flight.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U5-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use the present perfect to talk about experiences in our life up to now. We don't say when they happened: I have visited Abha. (sometime in my life) Form: have / has + past participle. Regular verbs: past participle = -ed (visited, tried). Irregular verbs have special forms: be → been, see → seen, eat → eaten, fly → flown, ride → ridden, swim → swum.","on_screen":"I / you / we / they + have ('ve) + past participle • he / she / it + has ('s) + past participle • Have you ever…? – Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I've ridden a camel in the desert. My sister has never seen snow. Have you ever tried scuba diving?","on_screen":"I've ridden a camel in the desert. / My sister has never seen snow. / Have you ever tried scuba diving?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have went to Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “I have been to Abha.” Use the past participle (been), not the past simple.","on_screen":"✗ I have went to Abha.   ✓ I have been to Abha.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I've ridden a camel.\" Do we know when? … Think! … No – only that it happened in my life. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I have visited Madinah\" and \"I've never seen snow.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I have visited Madinah\" and \"I've never seen snow.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم المضارع التام للتحدث عن التجارب في حياتنا حتى الآن دون ذكر الوقت: I have visited Abha.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have went to Abha. — الصحيح: I have been to Abha.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I have visited Madinah وI've never seen snow."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Uncle Fahad's Adventures","body":"Omar's uncle Fahad is a pilot, so he has visited many countries. He has worked for the same airline for fifteen years, and he has never missed a flight.\nHe has flown over the Alps, and he has seen the Northern Lights in Norway.\n\"Have you ever eaten anything strange?\" Omar asked.\n\"Yes, I have. I've tried durian, the smelliest fruit in the world!\" Uncle Fahad laughed.\n\"Have you ever been scared on a plane?\"\n\"Never! But I've been very tired many times.\"\nOmar has never flown in a plane, but he has traveled by train to Riyadh.\n\"One day, I'll fly too,\" he said. \"Maybe I'll be a pilot like you and see the whole world!\"","word_count":117,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ been to Makkah three times.","options":["am","have","has","had"],"answer":"have","explanation":"I / you / we / they → have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have مع الجمع."},{"q":"My uncle ___ climbed Jabal Sawda.","options":["has","is","had been","have"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has + past participle.","explanation_ar":"has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"Have you ever ___ a horse?","options":["rode","ride","ridden","riding"],"answer":"ridden","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"___ you ever tasted camel milk?","options":["Has","Are","Have","Did"],"answer":"Have","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"I've ___ seen a whale. I want to see one!","options":["always","ever","once","never"],"answer":"never","explanation":"never = not at any time (no other \"not\").","explanation_ar":"never نفي."},{"q":"She has ___ a famous footballer.","options":["meet","meeted","meets","met"],"answer":"met","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the past participle. Word bank: eaten, swum, flown","items":[{"q":"eat → I have ______ dates from Al-Ahsa.","options":[],"answer":"eaten","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"fly → We have ______ over the Red Sea.","options":[],"answer":"flown","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"swim → Has he ever ______ in a lake?","options":[],"answer":"swum","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make questions with Have you ever…? or Has … ever…?","items":[{"q":"you / see a shooting star  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Have you ever seen a shooting star?","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"your dad / drive a truck  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Has your dad ever driven a truck?","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"your friends / visit Jeddah  (question)","options":[],"answer":"Have your friends ever visited Jeddah?","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your experiences.","items":[{"q":"Have you ever ridden a camel?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. / No, I haven't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever eaten something very spicy?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. I've eaten very spicy chicken.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever been on a plane?","options":[],"answer":"No, I haven't.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Has your best friend ever visited another country?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, he has. He's been to Egypt.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I have never done is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Something I have never done is scuba diving.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Find someone who…","items":[{"q":"Write 4 \"Have you ever…?\" questions for a class survey.","options":[],"answer":"Have you ever ridden a zip line? Have you ever seen snow? Have you ever tried sushi? Have you ever met a pilot?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask 3 classmates. Write their answers with has/hasn't.","options":[],"answer":"Saad has seen snow. Ali hasn't ridden a zip line. Fahad has met a pilot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about things you have done many times.","options":[],"answer":"I've visited my grandpa many times. I've played chess hundreds of times.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"been"},{"label":"seen"},{"label":"eaten"},{"label":"flown"},{"label":"ridden"},{"label":"swum"},{"label":"tried"},{"label":"met"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We ___ visited the National Museum.","options":["are","had","has","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"I / you / we / they → have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have مع الجمع."},{"q":"My little brother ___ never seen the sea.","options":["have","is","has","had"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has + past participle.","explanation_ar":"has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"Have you ever ___ a roller coaster?","options":["ride","rided","ridden","rode"],"answer":"ridden","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["Has your mom ever went to Jordan?","Has your mom ever been to Jordan?","Did your mom ever been to Jordan?","Have your mom ever been to Jordan?"],"answer":"Has your mom ever been to Jordan?","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"","options":["I've never tried scuba diving.","I don't have never tried scuba diving.","I've never not tried scuba diving.","I've never try scuba diving."],"answer":"I've never tried scuba diving.","explanation":"never = not at any time (no other \"not\").","explanation_ar":"never نفي."},{"q":"Have you ever seen a falcon? – Yes, I ___.","options":["am","saw","did","have"],"answer":"have","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"","options":["They have eat at that restaurant twice.","They has eaten at that restaurant twice.","They have eaten at that restaurant twice.","They have ate at that restaurant twice."],"answer":"They have eaten at that restaurant twice.","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"Has Lina ever ___ a cake by herself?","options":["baking","baked","bake","bakes"],"answer":"baked","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"","options":["She's meeted a real astronaut!","She's met a real astronaut!","She have met a real astronaut!","She's meet a real astronaut!"],"answer":"She's met a real astronaut!","explanation":"he / she / it → has + past participle.","explanation_ar":"has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"Have your parents ever traveled abroad? – No, they ___.","options":["haven't","didn't","hasn't","don't"],"answer":"haven't","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Omar interviewing his uncle Fahad, a pilot in uniform, in a living room full of travel photos from around the world. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar interviewing his uncle Fahad, a pilot in uniform, in a living room full of travel photos from around the world"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows experience (something that happens to you that you remember); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing experience: something that happens to you that you remember"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ever (at any time in your life (in questions)); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ever: at any time in your life (in questions)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows never (not at any time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing never: not at any time"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows once (one time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing once: one time"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W01","script":"experience. experience. Flying in a hot-air balloon was a great experience.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W02","script":"ever. ever. Have you ever seen a shooting star?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W03","script":"never. never. I have never been to Japan.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-W04","script":"once. once. I have ridden a horse once.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-T1","script":"Omar's uncle Fahad is a pilot, so he has visited many countries. He has worked for the same airline for fifteen years, and he has never missed a flight. He has flown over the Alps, and he has seen the Northern Lights in Norway. \"Have you ever eaten anything strange?\" Omar asked. \"Yes, I have. I've tried durian, the smelliest fruit in the world!\" Uncle Fahad laughed. \"Have you ever been scared on a plane?\" \"Never! But I've been very tired many times.\" Omar has never flown in a plane, but he has traveled by train to Riyadh. \"One day, I'll fly too,\" he said. \"Maybe I'll be a pilot like you and see the whole world!\"","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Have You Ever Flown? The Present Perfect for Experiences”. Let’s learn present perfect (have/has + past participle) with ever and never together. Listen to the start of “Uncle Fahad's Adventures”: Omar's uncle Fahad is a pilot, so he has visited many countries. He has worked for the same airline for fifteen years, and he has never missed a flight. Look at the green words. We use the present perfect to talk about experiences in our life up to now. We don't say when they happened: I have visited Abha. (sometime in my life) Form: have / has + past participle. Regular verbs: past participle = -ed (visited, tried). Irregular verbs have special forms: be → been, see → seen, eat → eaten, fly → flown, ride → ridden, swim → swum. Here are some examples. I've ridden a camel in the desert. My sister has never seen snow. Have you ever tried scuba diving? Be careful! Some learners say: “I have went to Abha.” That’s not right. We say: “I have been to Abha.” Use the past participle (been), not the past simple. Quick check: \"I've ridden a camel.\" Do we know when? … Think! … No – only that it happened in my life. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I have visited Madinah\" and \"I've never seen snow.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2","title":"I've Been to Abha. I Went There Last Year.","objectives":["Students will be able to use the present perfect for experiences without a time and the past simple with a finished time.","Students will be able to ask a present perfect question and follow up with a past simple question.","I can say \"I've been to Abha. I went there last summer.\"","I can ask \"Have you ever…? When did you…?\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع التام للتجارب دون وقت والماضي البسيط مع وقت منتهٍ.","سيتمكن الطلاب من طرح سؤال بالمضارع التام ثم سؤال متابعة بالماضي البسيط.","أستطيع أن أقول I've been to Abha. I went there last summer.","أستطيع أن أسأل Have you ever…? When did you…?"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"twice","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/twaɪs/","definition":"two times","arabic":"مرتين","example":"We have visited Madinah twice.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W01"},{"word":"try","pos":"verb","ipa":"/traɪ/","definition":"to do or taste something to see if you like it","arabic":"يجرّب","example":"Have you ever tried mango juice with mint?","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W02"},{"word":"taste","pos":"verb","ipa":"/teɪst/","definition":"to put food in your mouth to know its flavor","arabic":"يتذوق","example":"Taste the soup before you add salt.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W03"},{"word":"roller coaster","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈroʊlɚ ˈkoʊstɚ/","definition":"a fast ride with steep ups and downs at a theme park","arabic":"قطار الملاهي السريع","example":"The roller coaster was so fast!","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Present perfect = an experience in your life, no specific time: I've been to Abha.\nPast simple = a finished action at a specific time (yesterday, last year, in 2023, two days ago): I went to Abha last summer.\nWe often start with the present perfect and then give details with the past simple: \"Have you ever ridden a zip line?\" \"Yes, I have.\" \"When did you ride it?\" \"I rode it last August.\"","examples":["I've seen the Kaaba. I saw it for the first time in 2022.","Have you ever met a famous person? – Yes, I met a famous footballer last month.","My dad has been to China. He went there for work.","We visited the zoo yesterday.","When did you try sushi? – I tried it two weeks ago.","She has never ridden a horse.","I lost my phone last week, but I found it the next day.","Where did you see the dolphins? – In the Red Sea."],"common_errors":["✗ I have seen him yesterday. → ✓ I saw him yesterday. (yesterday = finished time → past simple.)","✗ Did you ever eat camel meat? → ✓ Have you ever eaten camel meat? (Life experience → present perfect.)","✗ When have you gone to Abha? → ✓ When did you go to Abha? (When asks for a time → past simple.)","✗ I've been to Egypt in 2023. → ✓ I went to Egypt in 2023. (A year = finished time → past simple.)"],"arabic":"المضارع التام للتجربة دون ذكر وقت: I've been to Abha.\nالماضي البسيط مع وقت محدد منتهٍ: I went to Abha last summer.\nنبدأ غالبًا بالمضارع التام ثم نسأل عن التفاصيل بالماضي البسيط: When did you go?\nلا نستخدم المضارع التام مع yesterday أو last year أو in 2023."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I've Been to Abha. I Went There Last Year.”. Let’s learn present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U5-LS2 | I've Been to Abha. I Went There Last Year.","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I've tried scuba diving. I tried it in 2024. I haven't seen that film. I didn't see it yesterday. Have you ever been to Al-Ula? – Yes. – When did you go? – Last winter.","on_screen":"I've tried scuba diving. I tried it in 2024. | I haven't seen that film. I didn't see it yesterday. | Have you ever been to Al-Ula? – Yes. – When did you go? – Last winter.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Present perfect = an experience in your life, no specific time: I've been to Abha. Past simple = a finished action at a specific time (yesterday, last year, in 2023, two days ago): I went to Abha last summer.","on_screen":"present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…?","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I've seen the Kaaba. I saw it for the first time in 2022. Have you ever met a famous person? – Yes, I met a famous footballer last month. My dad has been to China. He went there for work.","on_screen":"I've seen the Kaaba. I saw it for the first time in 2022. / Have you ever met a famous person? – Yes, I met a famous footballer last month. / My dad has been to China. He went there for work.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have seen him yesterday.” That’s not right. We say: “I saw him yesterday.” yesterday = finished time → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ I have seen him yesterday.   ✓ I saw him yesterday.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I've been to Abha.\" Do we know when? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've been to Abha. I went there last summer.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I've been to Abha. I went there last summer.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…?.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المضارع التام للتجربة دون ذكر وقت: I've been to Abha.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have seen him yesterday. — الصحيح: I saw him yesterday.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I've been to Abha. I went there last summer."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"I ___ to Riyadh three times.","options":["went","have been","was going","have gone yesterday"],"answer":"have been","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"I ___ to Riyadh last month.","options":["have gone","have been","go","went"],"answer":"went","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"___ did you visit Al-Ula? – Last winter.","options":["When","How long","Have","Ever"],"answer":"When","explanation":"When did…? asks for a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"When did ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Have you ever seen a camel race? – Yes, I ___ one last year.","options":["have seen","saw","seen","see"],"answer":"saw","explanation":"Ask \"Have you ever…?\" then follow up with \"When/Where did…?\"","explanation_ar":"سؤال متابعة."},{"q":"My cousin ___ never flown in a plane.","options":["did","was","has","have"],"answer":"has","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"We ___ the museum two days ago.","options":["visit","have visit","visited","have visited"],"answer":"visited","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Present perfect or past simple? Write the correct form. Word bank: bought, Have, have never eaten","items":[{"q":"I ______ (never / eat) octopus.","options":[],"answer":"have never eaten","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"My dad ______ (buy) a new car in 2025.","options":[],"answer":"bought","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"______ you ever ______ (ride) a donkey?","options":[],"answer":"Have","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"I have seen a big falcon yesterday.","options":[],"answer":"I saw a big falcon yesterday.","explanation":"have seen → saw. Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: have seen → saw. الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Did you ever eaten durian?","options":[],"answer":"Have you ever eaten durian?","explanation":"Did → Have. Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Did → Have. التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"When have you arrive in Jeddah?","options":[],"answer":"When did you arrive in Jeddah?","explanation":"have → did. When did…? asks for a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: have → did. When did ← الماضي البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Ask and answer with a follow-up question.","items":[{"q":"Have you ever been to a theme park? (When did you go?)","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. I went to one in Riyadh last year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever cooked a meal? (What did you cook?)","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. I cooked pasta last Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever won a prize? (What did you win?)","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. I won a medal for reading in 2025.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever been to a wedding? (Whose wedding was it?)","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. It was my uncle's wedding.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Have you ever seen the sea? (Where did you see it?)","options":[],"answer":"Yes, I have. I saw it in Jeddah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Experience interview.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 \"Have you ever…?\" questions and 3 follow-up questions.","options":[],"answer":"Have you ever flown? When did you fly? Have you ever met a pilot? Where did you meet him? Have you ever been camping? Where did you camp?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Interview a partner. Write his answers in 3 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"He has flown to Cairo. He flew there last summer. He has never been camping.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about your most exciting experience and when it happened.","options":[],"answer":"The most exciting thing I've done is a zip line. I did it in Abha last year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…?.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"you / ever / ride a camel / ?"},{"cue":"I / never / see snow / +"},{"cue":"she / ever / fly in a plane / ?"},{"cue":"we / visit / Madinah / +"},{"cue":"he / never / eat sushi / +"},{"cue":"they / ever / swim in the sea / ?"},{"cue":"my dad / try / scuba diving / +"},{"cue":"you / ever / meet a famous person / ?"},{"cue":"I / never / be to Europe / +"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My grandparents ___ to Makkah many times.","options":["were going","go","have been","went last year"],"answer":"have been","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"My grandparents ___ to Makkah last Ramadan.","options":["go","have been","have gone","went"],"answer":"went","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["When did you started school?","When did you start school?","When have you started school?","When you started school?"],"answer":"When did you start school?","explanation":"When did…? asks for a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"When did ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Have you ever tried mango ice cream? – Yes, I ___ it last week.","options":["tried it have","tried","have tried","try"],"answer":"tried","explanation":"Ask \"Have you ever…?\" then follow up with \"When/Where did…?\"","explanation_ar":"سؤال متابعة."},{"q":"","options":["I've never seen that film.","I've never saw that film.","I never saw that film yesterday.","I haven't never seen that film."],"answer":"I've never seen that film.","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"","options":["We have watched the game on Friday.","We watched the game on Friday.","We have watch the game on Friday.","We watch the game on Friday last."],"answer":"We watched the game on Friday.","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Which sentence is correct?","options":["She visited Egypt twice ever.","She has visit Egypt twice.","She has visited Egypt in 2023.","She has visited Egypt twice."],"answer":"She has visited Egypt twice.","explanation":"Experience, no time → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة دون وقت ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"Where ___ you see the dolphins? – In the Red Sea.","options":["are","have","do","did"],"answer":"did","explanation":"When did…? asks for a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"When did ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["I have lose my keys yesterday.","I lose my keys yesterday.","I lost my keys yesterday.","I have lost my keys yesterday."],"answer":"I lost my keys yesterday.","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Have you ever been to a camel race? – ___","options":["Yes, I went to one last spring.","Yes, I go to one last spring.","Yes, I have been to one last spring.","Yes, I have go to one last spring."],"answer":"Yes, I went to one last spring.","explanation":"Ask \"Have you ever…?\" then follow up with \"When/Where did…?\"","explanation_ar":"سؤال متابعة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two speech bubbles between Lina and Sara: one shows a general experience (a zip line icon), the other a calendar page \"last August\" with a photo of the same zip line. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two speech bubbles between Lina and Sara: one shows a general experience (a zip line icon), the other a calendar page \"last August\" with a photo of the same zip line"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…?: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Have You Ever…?”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows twice (two times); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing twice: two times"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows try (to do or taste something to see if you like it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing try: to do or taste something to see if you like it"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows taste (to put food in your mouth to know its flavor); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing taste: to put food in your mouth to know its flavor"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows roller coaster (a fast ride with steep ups and downs at a theme park); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing roller coaster: a fast ride with steep ups and downs at a theme park"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W01","script":"twice. twice. We have visited Madinah twice.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W02","script":"try. try. Have you ever tried mango juice with mint?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W03","script":"taste. taste. Taste the soup before you add salt.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-W04","script":"roller coaster. roller coaster. The roller coaster was so fast!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “I've Been to Abha. I Went There Last Year.”. Let’s learn present perfect (experience, no time) vs past simple (finished time); follow-up questions with When/Where did…? together. Remember these patterns: I've tried scuba diving. I tried it in 2024. I haven't seen that film. I didn't see it yesterday. Have you ever been to Al-Ula? – Yes. – When did you go? – Last winter. Present perfect = an experience in your life, no specific time: I've been to Abha. Past simple = a finished action at a specific time (yesterday, last year, in 2023, two days ago): I went to Abha last summer. Here are some examples. I've seen the Kaaba. I saw it for the first time in 2022. Have you ever met a famous person? – Yes, I met a famous footballer last month. My dad has been to China. He went there for work. Be careful! Some learners say: “I have seen him yesterday.” That’s not right. We say: “I saw him yesterday.” yesterday = finished time → past simple. Quick check: \"I've been to Abha.\" Do we know when? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I've been to Abha. I went there last summer.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3","title":"Exciting or Excited? -ing and -ed Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to use -ing adjectives to describe things and -ed adjectives to describe feelings.","Students will be able to describe experiences with precise adjectives such as unforgettable.","I can say \"The ride was exciting, and I was excited.\"","I can describe my experiences with interesting adjectives."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صفات ing لوصف الأشياء وصفات ed لوصف المشاعر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف التجارب بصفات دقيقة مثل unforgettable.","أستطيع أن أقول The ride was exciting, and I was excited.","أستطيع أن أصف تجاربي بصفات مثيرة للاهتمام."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"zip line","pos":"noun","ipa":"/zɪp laɪn/","definition":"a cable you slide along high in the air","arabic":"الحبل المنزلق (زِب لاين)","example":"We rode a zip line over the valley.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W01"},{"word":"scuba diving","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskubə ˈdaɪvɪŋ/","definition":"swimming underwater with air tanks","arabic":"الغوص بأسطوانات الهواء","example":"My uncle has gone scuba diving in the Red Sea.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W02"},{"word":"exciting","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsaɪtɪŋ/","definition":"making you feel very happy and full of energy","arabic":"مثير","example":"The match was really exciting.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W03"},{"word":"frightening","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfraɪtənɪŋ/","definition":"making you feel afraid","arabic":"مخيف","example":"The storm was frightening.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W04"},{"word":"unforgettable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌʌnfɚˈɡɛtəbəl/","definition":"so good or special that you can't forget it","arabic":"لا يُنسى","example":"Our trip to Al-Ula was unforgettable.","image_id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"-ing adjectives describe the thing or experience that causes a feeling: The roller coaster was exciting. The film was boring.\n-ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was excited. My brother was bored.\nPairs: exciting/excited • frightening/frightened • boring/bored • interesting/interested • tiring/tired • amazing/amazed • surprising/surprised. unforgettable = you can't forget it.\nWord families: excite: exciting (adj), excited (adj), excitement (n) | frighten: frightening (adj), frightened (adj), fright (n) | bore: boring (adj), bored (adj), boredom (n) | interest: interesting (adj), interested (adj), interest (n) | surprise: surprising (adj), surprised (adj), surprise (n)\nCollocations/phrases: an exciting ride • a frightening storm • an interesting experience • an unforgettable trip • feel excited • get bored","examples":["The zip line was exciting!","I was excited before the trip.","The thunderstorm was frightening.","My little sister was frightened of the dark.","This documentary about sharks is interesting.","Are you interested in scuba diving?","The long walk was tiring, and we were tired.","Our first trip abroad was unforgettable."],"common_errors":["✗ I am boring in this lesson. → ✓ I am bored in this lesson. (The person feels → -ed.)","✗ The film was very interested. → ✓ The film was very interesting. (The thing → -ing.)","✗ I'm interesting in science. → ✓ I'm interested in science. (Feeling → interested in.)","✗ The roller coaster was excited. → ✓ The roller coaster was exciting. (The ride causes the feeling → -ing.)"],"arabic":"صفات ing تصف الشيء أو التجربة التي تسبب الشعور: The ride was exciting (مثيرة).\nصفات ed تصف شعور الشخص: I was excited (متحمس).\nانتبه: I am bored (أشعر بالملل) وليس I am boring (أنا ممل!).\nنقول interested in: I'm interested in science."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Exciting or Excited? -ing and -ed Adjectives”. Let’s learn -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U5-LS3 | Exciting or Excited? -ing and -ed Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. zip line: a cable you slide along high in the air. scuba diving: swimming underwater with air tanks. exciting: making you feel very happy and full of energy.","on_screen":"zip line | scuba diving | exciting","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"-ing adjectives describe the thing or experience that causes a feeling: The roller coaster was exciting. The film was boring. -ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was excited. My brother was bored.","on_screen":"-ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The zip line was exciting! I was excited before the trip. The thunderstorm was frightening.","on_screen":"The zip line was exciting! / I was excited before the trip. / The thunderstorm was frightening.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I am boring in this lesson.” That’s not right. We say: “I am bored in this lesson.” The person feels → -ed.","on_screen":"✗ I am boring in this lesson.   ✓ I am bored in this lesson.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"The film was boring.\" Is \"boring\" about the film or about me? … Think! … About the film. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The ride was exciting, and I was excited.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"The ride was exciting, and I was excited.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صفات ing تصف الشيء أو التجربة التي تسبب الشعور: The ride was exciting (مثيرة).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I am boring in this lesson. — الصحيح: I am bored in this lesson.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول The ride was exciting, and I was excited."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The roller coaster was very ___.","options":["excited","excitement","exciting","excite"],"answer":"exciting","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"I was ___ when I saw the big snake.","options":["frightened","fright","frighten","frightening"],"answer":"frightened","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"The lesson was long and ___.","options":["boredom","bored","bore","boring"],"answer":"boring","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"My brother is ___ in robots.","options":["interest","interested","interesting","interests"],"answer":"interested","explanation":"interested in something.","explanation_ar":"interested in."},{"q":"After the long hike, we were very ___.","options":["tiredness","tire","tired","tiring"],"answer":"tired","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"Our trip to the Farasan Islands was ___. We'll never forget it!","options":["unforgettable","unforgotten","forgettable","forgetful"],"answer":"unforgettable","explanation":"Choose the experience word that fits.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the sentence halves.","items":[{"q":"The documentary was","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"interesting.","explanation":"The documentary was → interesting.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"I was really","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"surprised by the news.","explanation":"I was really → surprised by the news.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"The dark cave was","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"frightening.","explanation":"The dark cave was → frightening.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"My little brother got","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"bored in the car.","explanation":"My little brother got → bored in the car.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"The football final was","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"exciting.","explanation":"The football final was → exciting.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"After the race, the runners felt","options":["bored in the car.","interesting.","exciting.","tired.","frightening.","surprised by the news."],"answer":"tired.","explanation":"After the race, the runners felt → tired.. The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe your experiences.","items":[{"q":"The most exciting thing I have ever done is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most exciting thing I have ever done is a zip line in Abha.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I felt frightened when ___.","options":[],"answer":"I felt frightened when the plane shook.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I'm interested in ___.","options":[],"answer":"I'm interested in space.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A boring thing for me is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A boring thing for me is waiting at the doctor's.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An unforgettable day in my life was ___.","options":[],"answer":"An unforgettable day in my life was my first Umrah.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Experience review.","items":[{"q":"Write a short review of a trip or a ride with 2 -ing adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"The safari park was amazing. The lions were frightening but beautiful.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about how you felt with -ed adjectives.","options":[],"answer":"I was excited in the morning. I was tired at the end of the day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with \"interested in\".","options":[],"answer":"My cousin is interested in photography.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"exciting","category":"adjective","family":"excite"},{"word":"excited","category":"adjective","family":"excite"},{"word":"excitement","category":"noun","family":"excite"},{"word":"frightening","category":"adjective","family":"frighten"},{"word":"frightened","category":"adjective","family":"frighten"},{"word":"fright","category":"noun","family":"frighten"},{"word":"boring","category":"adjective","family":"bore"},{"word":"bored","category":"adjective","family":"bore"},{"word":"boredom","category":"noun","family":"bore"},{"word":"interesting","category":"adjective","family":"interest"},{"word":"interested","category":"adjective","family":"interest"},{"word":"interest","category":"noun","family":"interest"},{"word":"surprising","category":"adjective","family":"surprise"},{"word":"surprised","category":"adjective","family":"surprise"},{"word":"surprise","category":"noun","family":"surprise"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The magic show was ___.","options":["amazement","amazing","amaze","amazed"],"answer":"amazing","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"We were ___ when we heard the news.","options":["surprises","surprised","surprising","surprise"],"answer":"surprised","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"","options":["I'm boring. Let's play a game.","I'm bore. Let's play a game.","I'm bored. Let's play a game.","I'm boredom. Let's play a game."],"answer":"I'm bored. Let's play a game.","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"","options":["The book about volcanoes is interests.","The book about volcanoes is interested.","The book about volcanoes is interesting.","The book about volcanoes is interest."],"answer":"The book about volcanoes is interesting.","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"Are you interested ___ history?","options":["at","on","about of","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"interested in something.","explanation_ar":"interested in."},{"q":"The storm was ___. Everyone stayed inside.","options":["frightening","frighten","frightened","fright"],"answer":"frightening","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"My dad was ___ after a long day at work.","options":["tiredly","tire","tiring","tired"],"answer":"tired","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"The trip was so special. It was ___.","options":["unforgotten","forgettable","forgetful","unforgettable"],"answer":"unforgettable","explanation":"Choose the experience word that fits.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["The kids were excited about the zip line.","The kids were excitement about the zip line.","The kids were exciting about the zip line.","The kids were excite about the zip line."],"answer":"The kids were excited about the zip line.","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"Which sentence describes a feeling?","options":["The cave was dark.","The ride was long.","I was frightened.","The film was frightening."],"answer":"I was frightened.","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A theme park split image: a fast roller coaster labeled with a lightning bolt (exciting) and a boy on it with wide eyes and a big smile (excited); a dark cave (frightening) and a scared girl (frightened). Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A theme park split image: a fast roller coaster labeled with a lightning bolt (exciting) and a boy on it with wide eyes and a big smile (excited); a dark cave (frightening) and a scared girl (frightened)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows zip line (a cable you slide along high in the air); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing zip line: a cable you slide along high in the air"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows scuba diving (swimming underwater with air tanks); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing scuba diving: swimming underwater with air tanks"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows exciting (making you feel very happy and full of energy); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing exciting: making you feel very happy and full of energy"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows frightening (making you feel afraid); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing frightening: making you feel afraid"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows unforgettable (so good or special that you can't forget it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing unforgettable: so good or special that you can't forget it"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W01","script":"zip line. zip line. We rode a zip line over the valley.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W02","script":"scuba diving. scuba diving. My uncle has gone scuba diving in the Red Sea.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W03","script":"exciting. exciting. The match was really exciting.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W04","script":"frightening. frightening. The storm was frightening.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-W05","script":"unforgettable. unforgettable. Our trip to Al-Ula was unforgettable.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Exciting or Excited? -ing and -ed Adjectives”. Let’s learn -ing and -ed adjectives (exciting/excited, frightening/frightened, boring/bored, interesting/interested, tiring/tired); experience words together. Meet some new words. zip line: a cable you slide along high in the air. scuba diving: swimming underwater with air tanks. exciting: making you feel very happy and full of energy. -ing adjectives describe the thing or experience that causes a feeling: The roller coaster was exciting. The film was boring. -ed adjectives describe how a person feels: I was excited. My brother was bored. Here are some examples. The zip line was exciting! I was excited before the trip. The thunderstorm was frightening. Be careful! Some learners say: “I am boring in this lesson.” That’s not right. We say: “I am bored in this lesson.” The person feels → -ed. Quick check: \"The film was boring.\" Is \"boring\" about the film or about me? … Think! … About the film. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The ride was exciting, and I was excited.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4","title":"Two Friends Went There Too: to/too/two and there/their/they're","objectives":["Students will be able to choose correctly between to, too and two.","Students will be able to choose correctly between there, their and they're.","I can write \"Two friends went to the park too.\"","I can write \"They're at their house over there.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار الصحيح بين to وtoo وtwo.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار الصحيح بين there وtheir وthey're.","أستطيع أن أكتب Two friends went to the park too.","أستطيع أن أكتب They're at their house over there."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪriəns/","definition":"something that happens to you that you remember","arabic":"تجربة","example":"Flying in a hot-air balloon was a great experience.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ever","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɛvɚ/","definition":"at any time in your life (in questions)","arabic":"من قبل / في أي وقت","example":"Have you ever seen a shooting star?","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time","arabic":"أبدًا / قطّ","example":"I have never been to Japan.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"once","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/wʌns/","definition":"one time","arabic":"مرة واحدة","example":"I have ridden a horse once.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"twice","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/twaɪs/","definition":"two times","arabic":"مرتين","example":"We have visited Madinah twice.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"try","pos":"verb","ipa":"/traɪ/","definition":"to do or taste something to see if you like it","arabic":"يجرّب","example":"Have you ever tried mango juice with mint?","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"These words sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (homophones).\nto = direction or before a verb (go to school, want to go) • too = also, or more than enough (I'm hungry too; It's too hot) • two = the number 2.\nthere = a place or there is/are (over there; there are two cats) • their = belongs to them (their car) • they're = they are (They're happy).\nto → direction/before a verb • too → also/very much • two → 2\nthere → place / there is/are\ntheir → possession (their bags)\nthey're → they are (contraction)","examples":["We went to the zoo.","I want to try scuba diving.","My brother wants to come too.","The tea is too hot to drink.","I've been to Madinah two times.","Look over there! A rainbow!","My cousins visited their grandparents.","They're going to Abha next week."],"common_errors":["✗ I want too go. → ✓ I want to go. (Before a verb → to.)","✗ I like dates to. → ✓ I like dates too. (also → too.)","✗ Their are two cats in the garden. → ✓ There are two cats in the garden. (there is/are → there.)","✗ There going to the park. → ✓ They're going to the park. (they are → they're.)"],"arabic":"هذه الكلمات تُنطق بنفس الطريقة لكن معانيها مختلفة.\nto = إلى / قبل الفعل، too = أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم، two = الرقم 2.\nthere = هناك / there is، their = لهم/لهن (ملكية)، they're = they are."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Two Friends Went There Too: to/too/two and there/their/they're”. Let’s learn commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U5-LS4 | Two Friends Went There Too: to/too/two and there/their/they're","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"These words sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (homophones).","on_screen":"commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"These words sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (homophones). to = direction or before a verb (go to school, want to go) • too = also, or more than enough (I'm hungry too; It's too hot) • two = the number 2.","on_screen":"to → direction/before a verb • too → also/very much • two → 2 • there → place / there is/are • their → possession (their bags)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We went to the zoo. I want to try scuba diving. My brother wants to come too.","on_screen":"We went to the zoo. / I want to try scuba diving. / My brother wants to come too.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I want too go.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to go.” Before a verb → to.","on_screen":"✗ I want too go.   ✓ I want to go.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"They're\" means … ? … Think! … *they are*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Two friends went to the park too.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"Two friends went to the park too.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","هذه الكلمات تُنطق بنفس الطريقة لكن معانيها مختلفة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I want too go. — الصحيح: I want to go.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب Two friends went to the park too."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"A Message from Sara (editing passage)","body":"We went too Abha last weekend. My to cousins came two! There really funny. We stayed at they're house. Their was a beautiful view of the mountains.","word_count":27,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"We drove ___ the airport.","options":["two","toe","too","to"],"answer":"to","explanation":"to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"I have ___ brothers.","options":["two","to","too","tow"],"answer":"two","explanation":"two = the number 2.","explanation_ar":"two الرقم 2."},{"q":"This soup is ___ salty.","options":["to","tow","too","two"],"answer":"too","explanation":"too = also, or more than enough.","explanation_ar":"too تعني أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم."},{"q":"Put your bag over ___.","options":["their","there","thier","they're"],"answer":"there","explanation":"there = a place / there is, there are.","explanation_ar":"there للمكان."},{"q":"The children washed ___ hands.","options":["their","thier","they're","there"],"answer":"their","explanation":"their = belongs to them.","explanation_ar":"their للملكية."},{"q":"___ excited about the trip.","options":["There","They're","Their","Theyre"],"answer":"They're","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're = they are."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write to, too or two. Word bank: too, their, two, There, to, They're","items":[{"q":"I would like ______ see the Northern Lights.","options":[],"answer":"to","explanation":"to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"Can I come with you ______?","options":[],"answer":"too","explanation":"too = also, or more than enough.","explanation_ar":"too تعني أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم."},{"q":"We stayed in Abha for ______ nights.","options":[],"answer":"two","explanation":"two = the number 2.","explanation_ar":"two الرقم 2."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write there, their or they're. Word bank: too, their, two, There, to, They're","items":[{"q":"My cousins love ______ new house.","options":[],"answer":"their","explanation":"their = belongs to them.","explanation_ar":"their للملكية."},{"q":"______ is a big park near our school.","options":[],"answer":"There","explanation":"there = a place / there is, there are.","explanation_ar":"there للمكان."},{"q":"______ going to try the zip line.","options":[],"answer":"They're","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're = they are."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the trip message.","items":[{"q":"We went too Abha last weekend.","options":[],"answer":"We went to Abha last weekend.","explanation":"too → to. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: too → to. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"My to cousins came too! They're really funny.","options":[],"answer":"My two cousins came too! They're really funny.","explanation":"to → two. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: to → two. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"My two cousins came two! They're really funny.","options":[],"answer":"My two cousins came too! They're really funny.","explanation":"two → too. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: two → too. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"My two cousins came too! There really funny.","options":[],"answer":"My two cousins came too! They're really funny.","explanation":"There → They're. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: There → They're. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"We stayed at they're house. There was a beautiful view of the mountains.","options":[],"answer":"We stayed at their house. There was a beautiful view of the mountains.","explanation":"they're → their. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: they're → their. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"We stayed at their house. Their was a beautiful view of the mountains.","options":[],"answer":"We stayed at their house. There was a beautiful view of the mountains.","explanation":"Their → There. to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Their → There. to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write with homophones.","items":[{"q":"Write one sentence each with to, too and two.","options":[],"answer":"I went to the park. My brother came too. We stayed for two hours.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence each with there, their and they're.","options":[],"answer":"There is a museum in Riyadh. My friends love their school. They're very kind.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Make a mini-quiz of 2 sentences for a partner (leave a blank for the homophone).","options":[],"answer":"I'm ___ tired to play. (too) / ___ car is red. (Their)","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"to","clue":""},{"word":"too","clue":""},{"word":"two","clue":""},{"word":"there","clue":""},{"word":"their","clue":""},{"word":"they're","clue":""},{"word":"experience","clue":"something that happens to you that you remember"},{"word":"ever","clue":"at any time in your life (in questions)"},{"word":"never","clue":"not at any time"},{"word":"once","clue":"one time"},{"word":"twice","clue":"two times"},{"word":"try","clue":"to do or taste something to see if you like it"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"I'm going ___ visit my grandma.","options":["tow","too","two","to"],"answer":"to","explanation":"to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"Can I have ___ cookies, please?","options":["too","to","two","tow"],"answer":"two","explanation":"two = the number 2.","explanation_ar":"two الرقم 2."},{"q":"","options":["My sister likes camping too.","My sister likes camping two.","My sister likes camping to.","My sister likes camping tow."],"answer":"My sister likes camping too.","explanation":"too = also, or more than enough.","explanation_ar":"too تعني أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم."},{"q":"","options":["Their teacher is from Egypt.","Thier teacher is from Egypt.","They're teacher is from Egypt.","There teacher is from Egypt."],"answer":"Their teacher is from Egypt.","explanation":"their = belongs to them.","explanation_ar":"their للملكية."},{"q":"","options":["They're are three parks in our town.","Ther are three parks in our town.","There are three parks in our town.","Their are three parks in our town."],"answer":"There are three parks in our town.","explanation":"there = a place / there is, there are.","explanation_ar":"there للمكان."},{"q":"","options":["Theyre my best friends.","There my best friends.","Their my best friends.","They're my best friends."],"answer":"They're my best friends.","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're = they are."},{"q":"The box is ___ heavy for me to carry.","options":["tow","to","two","too"],"answer":"too","explanation":"too = also, or more than enough.","explanation_ar":"too تعني أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم."},{"q":"\"They're\" means ___.","options":["their is","they are","they were","there are"],"answer":"they are","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're = they are."},{"q":"","options":["We have been to Jeddah too times.","We have been too Jeddah two times.","We have been to Jeddah two times.","We have been two Jeddah to times."],"answer":"We have been to Jeddah two times.","explanation":"two = the number 2.","explanation_ar":"two الرقم 2."},{"q":"The birds are building ___ nest in the tree.","options":["there","their","thier","they're"],"answer":"their","explanation":"their = belongs to them.","explanation_ar":"their للملكية."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Have You Ever…?” that shows commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Have You Ever…?” that shows commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Two Friends Went There Too: to/too/two and there/their/they're”. Let’s learn commonly confused words: to / too / two and there / their / they're together. These words sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (homophones). These words sound the same but have different meanings and spellings (homophones). to = direction or before a verb (go to school, want to go) • too = also, or more than enough (I'm hungry too; It's too hot) • two = the number 2. Here are some examples. We went to the zoo. I want to try scuba diving. My brother wants to come too. Be careful! Some learners say: “I want too go.” That’s not right. We say: “I want to go.” Before a verb → to. Quick check: \"They're\" means … ? … Think! … *they are*. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"Two friends went to the park too.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5","title":"My Experience Map: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to interview classmates about experiences with follow-up questions.","Students will be able to write about their experiences using the present perfect, the past simple and precise adjectives.","I can interview a classmate about his experiences.","I can write about my experiences and my dreams."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من مقابلة زملائهم عن تجاربهم مع أسئلة المتابعة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من الكتابة عن تجاربهم بالمضارع التام والماضي البسيط والصفات الدقيقة.","أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع زميل عن تجاربه.","أستطيع أن أكتب عن تجاربي وأحلامي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"experience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪkˈspɪriəns/","definition":"something that happens to you that you remember","arabic":"تجربة","example":"Flying in a hot-air balloon was a great experience.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ever","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈɛvɚ/","definition":"at any time in your life (in questions)","arabic":"من قبل / في أي وقت","example":"Have you ever seen a shooting star?","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"never","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈnɛvɚ/","definition":"not at any time","arabic":"أبدًا / قطّ","example":"I have never been to Japan.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"once","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/wʌns/","definition":"one time","arabic":"مرة واحدة","example":"I have ridden a horse once.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"twice","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/twaɪs/","definition":"two times","arabic":"مرتين","example":"We have visited Madinah twice.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"try","pos":"verb","ipa":"/traɪ/","definition":"to do or taste something to see if you like it","arabic":"يجرّب","example":"Have you ever tried mango juice with mint?","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"taste","pos":"verb","ipa":"/teɪst/","definition":"to put food in your mouth to know its flavor","arabic":"يتذوق","example":"Taste the soup before you add salt.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"roller coaster","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈroʊlɚ ˈkoʊstɚ/","definition":"a fast ride with steep ups and downs at a theme park","arabic":"قطار الملاهي السريع","example":"The roller coaster was so fast!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"zip line","pos":"noun","ipa":"/zɪp laɪn/","definition":"a cable you slide along high in the air","arabic":"الحبل المنزلق (زِب لاين)","example":"We rode a zip line over the valley.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"scuba diving","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈskubə ˈdaɪvɪŋ/","definition":"swimming underwater with air tanks","arabic":"الغوص بأسطوانات الهواء","example":"My uncle has gone scuba diving in the Red Sea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"exciting","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪkˈsaɪtɪŋ/","definition":"making you feel very happy and full of energy","arabic":"مثير","example":"The match was really exciting.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"frightening","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈfraɪtənɪŋ/","definition":"making you feel afraid","arabic":"مخيف","example":"The storm was frightening.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"unforgettable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˌʌnfɚˈɡɛtəbəl/","definition":"so good or special that you can't forget it","arabic":"لا يُنسى","example":"Our trip to Al-Ula was unforgettable.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 5: the present perfect for experiences, the past simple for details with a time, -ing/-ed adjectives and the homophones to/too/two and there/their/they're.\nStart with an experience (present perfect), then add when, where and how it was (past simple + adjectives).\n✔ I've + past participle (experience)\n✔ past simple for details: when? where? how was it?\n✔ -ing (the thing) and -ed (the feeling) adjectives\n✔ to/too/two and there/their/they're","examples":["I've swum in the Red Sea.","I swam there last spring; it was amazing.","Have you ever been to a camel festival?","I was frightened on the roller coaster too.","My cousins have flown to Turkey two times.","They're going there again in June.","I haven't tried scuba diving yet.","Our trip to their farm was unforgettable."],"common_errors":["✗ I have rode a zip line last summer. → ✓ I rode a zip line last summer. (Finished time → past simple.)","✗ The zip line was excited. → ✓ The zip line was exciting. (The thing → -ing.)","✗ Their going to Makkah. → ✓ They're going to Makkah. (they are → they're.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع التام والماضي البسيط وصفات ing/ed والكلمات المتشابهة في النطق.\nنبدأ بالتجربة (المضارع التام) ثم نضيف التفاصيل: متى وأين وكيف كانت (الماضي البسيط).\nتذكّر: صفة ing للشيء وed للشعور."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Experience Map: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U5-LS5 | My Experience Map: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Experience bingo: walk around and ask \"Have you ever…?\" When someone says yes, ask a follow-up question (\"When did you…? How was it?\") and write his name and one detail in the bingo square.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 5: the present perfect for experiences, the past simple for details with a time, -ing/-ed adjectives and the homophones to/too/two and there/their/they're. Start with an experience (present perfect), then add when, where and how it was (past simple + adjectives).","on_screen":"✔ I've + past participle (experience) • ✔ past simple for details: when? where? how was it? • ✔ -ing (the thing) and -ed (the feeling) adjectives","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. I've swum in the Red Sea. I swam there last spring; it was amazing. Have you ever been to a camel festival?","on_screen":"I've swum in the Red Sea. / I swam there last spring; it was amazing. / Have you ever been to a camel festival?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I have rode a zip line last summer.” That’s not right. We say: “I rode a zip line last summer.” Finished time → past simple.","on_screen":"✗ I have rode a zip line last summer.   ✓ I rode a zip line last summer.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “The zip line was excited.”? … Think! … It should be “The zip line was exciting.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview a classmate about his experiences.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can interview a classmate about his experiences.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع التام والماضي البسيط وصفات ing/ed والكلمات المتشابهة في النطق.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I have rode a zip line last summer. — الصحيح: I rode a zip line last summer.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أجري مقابلة مع زميل عن تجاربه."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"My Experience Map – Adam","body":"I have lived in two countries: Malaysia and Saudi Arabia.\nI've tried many interesting foods. The strangest one was durian – I tasted it when I was six!\nI've been on a zip line too. I rode one in Abha last summer, and it was so exciting.\nMy parents have visited Makkah many times. They're planning to take me there next year.\nI have never seen snow, but I'm very interested in the Arctic.\nOne day, I want to go there!","word_count":81,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Adam's experience map. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Adam has lived in two countries.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam tasted durian when he was ten.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam rode a zip line in Abha last summer.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam thought the zip line was boring.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam's parents have visited Makkah many times.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Adam has seen snow many times.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “My Experience Map – Adam”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Adam ___ two countries.","options":["has live in","have lived in","has lived in","lived in last year"],"answer":"has lived in","explanation":"Experience (no time) → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"He ___ a zip line in Abha last summer.","options":["has ridden","has rode","rode","rides"],"answer":"rode","explanation":"Detail with a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل مع الوقت ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The zip line was so ___.","options":["exciting","excited","excitement","excite"],"answer":"exciting","explanation":"-ing (thing) / -ed (feeling).","explanation_ar":"ing للشيء وed للشعور."},{"q":"He's been on a zip line ___.","options":["tow","to","two","too"],"answer":"too","explanation":"to/too/two • there/their/they're.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"___ planning to take him to Makkah.","options":["They're","Theyre","There","Their"],"answer":"They're","explanation":"to/too/two • there/their/they're.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"The strangest food was durian. It was a strange ___.","options":["never","experience","ever","twice"],"answer":"experience","explanation":"Experience word.","explanation_ar":"كلمة التجربة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Experience bingo. Write names and details.","items":[{"q":"Has anyone ridden a horse? Write the name and a detail.","options":[],"answer":"Saad has ridden a horse. He rode one at his uncle's farm.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Has anyone seen a whale?","options":[],"answer":"Fahad has seen a whale. He saw it in Oman.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Has anyone won a competition?","options":[],"answer":"Turki has won a chess competition. He won it last year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Has anyone tried a strange food?","options":[],"answer":"Ali has tried snails. He tried them in France.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Has anyone never been on a plane?","options":[],"answer":"Rakan has never been on a plane.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write \"My Experience Map\".","items":[{"q":"Plan: 3 experiences, details, feelings, 1 thing you've never done.","options":[],"answer":"zip line (Abha, last summer, exciting); Umrah (2024, peaceful); camel ride (desert, frightening at first); never: scuba diving","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your experience map in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"I've done many exciting things. I've ridden a zip line. I rode it in Abha last summer, and I was so excited. I've been to Makkah too. We went there in 2024. I've never tried scuba diving, but I'm interested in it. One day, I want to dive in the Red Sea.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: present perfect vs past simple? -ing/-ed? to/too/two? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"I have went\" to \"I have been\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"experience","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ever","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"never","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"once","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"twice","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"try","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"taste","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"roller coaster","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"zip line","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"scuba diving","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"exciting","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"frightening","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"unforgettable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My brother ___ in a hot-air balloon.","options":["flew last year has","has flown","has flew","have flown"],"answer":"has flown","explanation":"Experience (no time) → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"My brother ___ in a hot-air balloon in 2024.","options":["flies","flew","has flown","has fly"],"answer":"flew","explanation":"Detail with a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل مع الوقت ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"The documentary was really ___.","options":["interesting","interested","interests","interest"],"answer":"interesting","explanation":"-ing (thing) / -ed (feeling).","explanation_ar":"ing للشيء وed للشعور."},{"q":"","options":["We've been there two times.","We've been their two times.","We've been they're two times.","We've been there too times."],"answer":"We've been there two times.","explanation":"to/too/two • there/their/they're.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"","options":["Have you ever taste saffron tea?","Have you ever tasted saffron tea yesterday?","Have you ever tasted saffron tea?","Did you ever tasted saffron tea?"],"answer":"Have you ever tasted saffron tea?","explanation":"Experience (no time) → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"I felt ___ when the plane landed safely.","options":["relief","relieving","relieved","relieve"],"answer":"relieved","explanation":"-ing (thing) / -ed (feeling).","explanation_ar":"ing للشيء وed للشعور."},{"q":"","options":["When you went to Al-Ula?","When did you went to Al-Ula?","When have you gone to Al-Ula?","When did you go to Al-Ula?"],"answer":"When did you go to Al-Ula?","explanation":"Detail with a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل مع الوقت ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"My friends visited ___ uncle in Dammam.","options":["their","they're","thier","there"],"answer":"their","explanation":"to/too/two • there/their/they're.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المتشابهة."},{"q":"","options":["I've never went to Europe.","I've never be to Europe.","I haven't never been to Europe.","I've never been to Europe."],"answer":"I've never been to Europe.","explanation":"Experience (no time) → present perfect.","explanation_ar":"التجربة ← المضارع التام."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for \"My Experience Map\":","options":["I tried camel milk ever.","I have taste camel milk at a farm last year.","I've tried camel milk; I tasted it at a farm in 2025.","I've tried camel milk in 2025 at a farm."],"answer":"I've tried camel milk; I tasted it at a farm in 2025.","explanation":"Detail with a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"التفاصيل مع الوقت ← الماضي البسيط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Adam pinning photos on an \"Experience Map\" of the world with strings: a zip line in Abha, durian in Malaysia, the sea in Jeddah, and a question mark over Japan. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Adam pinning photos on an \"Experience Map\" of the world with strings: a zip line in Abha, durian in Malaysia, the sea in Jeddah, and a question mark over Japan"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Have You Ever…?”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Have You Ever…?”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U5-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS5-T1","script":"I have lived in two countries: Malaysia and Saudi Arabia. I've tried many interesting foods. The strangest one was durian – I tasted it when I was six! I've been on a zip line too. I rode one in Abha last summer, and it was so exciting. My parents have visited Makkah many times. They're planning to take me there next year. I have never seen snow, but I'm very interested in the Arctic. One day, I want to go there!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U5-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Experience Map: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present perfect vs past simple, -ing/-ed adjectives and homophones (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Experience bingo: walk around and ask \"Have you ever…?\" When someone says yes, ask a follow-up question (\"When did you…? How was it?\") and write his name and one detail in the bingo square. Today you use all of Unit 5: the present perfect for experiences, the past simple for details with a time, -ing/-ed adjectives and the homophones to/too/two and there/their/they're. Start with an experience (present perfect), then add when, where and how it was (past simple + adjectives). Here are some examples. I've swum in the Red Sea. I swam there last spring; it was amazing. Have you ever been to a camel festival? Be careful! Some learners say: “I have rode a zip line last summer.” That’s not right. We say: “I rode a zip line last summer.” Finished time → past simple. Quick check: what is wrong with “The zip line was excited.”? … Think! … It should be “The zip line was exciting.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can interview a classmate about his experiences.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"I ___ ridden a camel twice.","options":["has","have","am","had"],"answer":"have","explanation":"I / you / we / they → have + past participle.","explanation_ar":"have مع الجمع."},{"q":"My aunt ___ been to Malaysia.","options":["have","is","did","has"],"answer":"has","explanation":"he / she / it → has + past participle.","explanation_ar":"has مع المفرد الغائب."},{"q":"Have you ever ___ a shark?","options":["saw","seen","see","seeing"],"answer":"seen","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"___ your brother ever won a prize?","options":["Has","Is","Did","Have"],"answer":"Has","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."},{"q":"","options":["I've never eaten sushi.","I've never not eaten sushi.","I don't have never eaten sushi.","I've never ate sushi."],"answer":"I've never eaten sushi.","explanation":"never = not at any time (no other \"not\").","explanation_ar":"never نفي."},{"q":"We ___ to Abha last summer.","options":["have gone","have been","go","went"],"answer":"went","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["When have you bought your bike?","When you bought your bike?","When did you buy your bike?","When did you bought your bike?"],"answer":"When did you buy your bike?","explanation":"When did…? asks for a time → past simple.","explanation_ar":"When did ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"Have you ever been to a theme park? – Yes, I ___ to one in Riyadh last year.","options":["went","have been","go","have went"],"answer":"went","explanation":"Ask \"Have you ever…?\" then follow up with \"When/Where did…?\"","explanation_ar":"سؤال متابعة."},{"q":"","options":["I have seen a falcon yesterday.","I have saw a falcon yesterday.","I saw a falcon yesterday.","I see a falcon yesterday."],"answer":"I saw a falcon yesterday.","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle has climbed many mountains in 2020.","My uncle has climbed many mountains.","My uncle climbed many mountains ever.","My uncle has climb many mountains."],"answer":"My uncle has climbed many mountains.","explanation":"Use the past participle (been, seen, eaten, flown).","explanation_ar":"التصريف الثالث."},{"q":"The ride was very ___.","options":["excite","excitement","excited","exciting"],"answer":"exciting","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"I was ___ when I heard the loud noise.","options":["fright","frightening","frightened","frighten"],"answer":"frightened","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"Are you interested ___ space?","options":["in","at","of","on"],"answer":"in","explanation":"interested in something.","explanation_ar":"interested in."},{"q":"","options":["The museum was interest.","The museum was interests.","The museum was interested.","The museum was interesting."],"answer":"The museum was interesting.","explanation":"The thing or experience → -ing adjective.","explanation_ar":"الشيء ← صفة ing."},{"q":"Our first Umrah was special. It was ___.","options":["unforgotten","forgettable","unforgettable","forgetful"],"answer":"unforgettable","explanation":"Choose the experience word that fits.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["I'm tired after the long journey.","I'm tire after the long journey.","I'm tiring after the long journey.","I'm tiredness after the long journey."],"answer":"I'm tired after the long journey.","explanation":"The person's feeling → -ed adjective.","explanation_ar":"شعور الشخص ← صفة ed."},{"q":"I want ___ learn French.","options":["tow","two","to","too"],"answer":"to","explanation":"to = direction or before a verb.","explanation_ar":"to للاتجاه أو قبل الفعل."},{"q":"The coffee is ___ hot. Wait a minute.","options":["tow","two","to","too"],"answer":"too","explanation":"too = also, or more than enough.","explanation_ar":"too تعني أيضًا أو أكثر من اللازم."},{"q":"","options":["We stayed at our uncle's farm for to days.","We stayed at our uncle's farm for two days.","We stayed at our uncle's farm for tow days.","We stayed at our uncle's farm for too days."],"answer":"We stayed at our uncle's farm for two days.","explanation":"two = the number 2.","explanation_ar":"two الرقم 2."},{"q":"","options":["Their is a big mall near my house.","Thier is a big mall near my house.","They're is a big mall near my house.","There is a big mall near my house."],"answer":"There is a big mall near my house.","explanation":"there = a place / there is, there are.","explanation_ar":"there للمكان."},{"q":"","options":["The boys forgot their books.","The boys forgot there books.","The boys forgot they're books.","The boys forgot thier books."],"answer":"The boys forgot their books.","explanation":"their = belongs to them.","explanation_ar":"their للملكية."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an experience report:","options":["I've visited the Red Sea Project in March.","I've visited the Red Sea Project; I went there in March.","I visited the Red Sea Project ever.","I have visit the Red Sea Project in March."],"answer":"I've visited the Red Sea Project; I went there in March.","explanation":"Finished time (yesterday, last…, ago, in + year) → past simple.","explanation_ar":"الوقت المنتهي ← الماضي البسيط."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"their going to there grandpa's house to.\"","options":["Their going to there grandpa's house too.","They're going to their grandpa's house too.","There going to their grandpa's house too.","They're going to there grandpa's house to."],"answer":"They're going to their grandpa's house too.","explanation":"they're = they are.","explanation_ar":"they're = they are."},{"q":"Have you ever been scuba diving? – No, I ___.","options":["hasn't","didn't","haven't","don't"],"answer":"haven't","explanation":"Questions about experience: Have you ever…?","explanation_ar":"السؤال عن التجربة."}],"theme_ar":"هل سبق لك أن…؟","essential_question_ar":"كيف تغيّرنا التجارب الجديدة؟","can_do":"I can talk about my life experiences with the present perfect and say when things happened with the past simple.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن تجاربي الحياتية بالمضارع التام وأقول متى حدثت الأشياء بالماضي البسيط."});
